 font-medium\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"377.7\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"td\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"py-2 tabular-nums text-right text-ink-muted\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"489w\\\"}]]}],\\\"$L1a\\\"]}]]}]]}],\\\"$L1b\\\"]}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1c:T63d,\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"This is a low power CPU, but massive power-hungry GPU build in a very compact P-ATX case that is even smaller than the Fractal Ridge. The CPU cooler used is the ID-Cooling IS 50x v3 which can handle the Ryzen 7 7800X3D as the CPU is very power efficient. This 10.8L case is wider than expected and designed to fit SFX or SFX-L PSUs. The Cooler Master SFX 850W is compact yet provides enough power for the 7900 XTX which pulls almost 500W during stress testing compared to 90W from the CPU. Performance is excellent with normal 7800X3D temperatures during idle and moderate load. During Cinebench testing, temps maxed out at 91C with about 300 MHz throttle-back, which is expected for air cooling. The power button is located unusually at the bottom near the front. Major case considerations include: it's a small niche maker with continuous stock issues, expensive ($179-189US plus $60US shipping from Croatia with 2-3 week delivery), and requires thermal/performance concessions typical of SFF builds. The case is good and flexible for mini-ITX, mATX, and full-size ATX motherboards but cannot fit E-ATX or BTX boards. Better suited for air-cooling; full-size 120mm AIO possible but limits GPU length. Can fit full-size ATX PSUs if length doesn't exceed 140mm. Likely the smallest case fitting full-size ATX motherboards. Mini-ITX boards preferred due to PCIe riser blocking additional ports, easier mATX FPANEL access, potential mini-ITX CPU cooler conflicts with power cables, and GPU fitting constraints. Overall a solid and flexible compact case with notable availability and cost trade-offs.\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"17:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null